    "result": "All tests pass! Here's a summary of the fixes I made:\n\n## Issues Fixed\n\n**1. Governance test failure** (`src/finetune/governance.test.js`):\n   - **Problem**: The test tried to import `APPROVAL_STATUSES` as a named export from `./index.js`, but it was only in the default export.\n   - **Fix**: Added named exports for the schema constants (`APPROVAL_STATUSES`, `DATA_SENSITIVITY_LEVELS`, `GOVERNANCE_SECTIONS`, `RISK_LEVELS`) at the top of `finetune/index.js`.\n\n**2. Eval test failure** (`src/eval/index.test.js`):\n   - **Problem**: The `toxicityMetric` function was receiving `references` as the second parameter (from `runEvaluations`), but was treating it as `bannedTerms`. This caused the references to be interpreted as toxic keywords, incorrectly flagging the outputs.\n   - **Fix**: Updated `toxicityMetric` signature to accept `references` as the second parameter (default empty array) and `bannedTerms` as the third parameter, maintaining the expected call pattern from `runEvaluations`.\n\nBoth fixes maintain backward compatibility and all 28 frai-core tests now pass, along with the 11 frai-gate tests.",
